Q7. Creating a Nested List Using HTML

A nested list is a list in which one list is placed inside another list. The given question requires River as the main item and the four rivers as its sub-items.

HTML Code
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Nested List</title>
</head>
<body>

<ul>
    <li>River
        <ul>
            <li>Ganga</li>
            <li>Yamuna</li>
            <li>Brahmaputra</li>
            <li>Narmada</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
</ul>

</body>
</html>
Output
River
Ganga
Yamuna
Brahmaputra
Narmada

The outer <ul> creates the main unordered list, while the inner <ul> creates the nested list.

Q8. Types of CSS

There are three main types of CSS used to apply styles to HTML documents: Inline CSS, Internal CSS, and External CSS.

1. Inline CSS

Inline CSS is written directly inside the style attribute of an HTML element.

Example
<p style="color: blue;">This is a paragraph.</p>
Advantages
Easy to apply to a single element.
Useful for quick or specific changes.
Disadvantage
It becomes difficult to maintain when many elements need styling.
2. Internal CSS

Internal CSS is written inside the <style> tag in the <head> section of an HTML document.

Example
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        p {
            color: green;
            font-size: 20px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <p>This is a paragraph.</p>
</body>
</html>

Internal CSS is useful when the styles are required for only one webpage.

3. External CSS

External CSS is written in a separate .css file and connected to the HTML file using the <link> element.

HTML file
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>

<body>
    <h1>My Website</h1>
</body>
</html>
CSS file — style.css
h1 {
    color: purple;
    text-align: center;
}

External CSS is useful for larger websites because the same CSS file can be used for multiple HTML pages.

Q9. Practical Understanding

HTML, CSS, and JavaScript have different roles in the development of a webpage. The assignment specifically asks to differentiate them according to their role and contribution to a website.

Technology	Main Role	What It Contributes
HTML	Structure	Creates headings, paragraphs, images, links, forms, etc.
CSS	Presentation	Controls colors, fonts, spacing, layout, and appearance
JavaScript	Behavior	Adds interaction and dynamic functionality
HTML

HTML provides the basic structure of a webpage. It tells the browser what elements should be present on the page.

For example:

<h1>My Portfolio</h1>
<p>Welcome to my portfolio.</p>
CSS

CSS makes the webpage look attractive. It controls the appearance and layout of HTML elements.

h1 {
    color: blue;
}
JavaScript

JavaScript adds behavior and interaction to the webpage.

function showMessage() {
    alert("Hello!");
}
Simple Example

We can understand these three technologies using a simple analogy:

HTML = Skeleton of the webpage
CSS = Clothes/Design of the webpage
JavaScript = Actions/Behavior of the webpage

Therefore, HTML creates the structure, CSS designs it, and JavaScript makes it interactive.

Q10.a. What is the role of Bootstrap in web development?

Bootstrap is a frontend framework used to create responsive and attractive websites more easily. It provides ready-made CSS classes and components such as buttons, forms, cards, navigation bars, and grids.

Its main role is to reduce development time and help developers create websites that work properly on different screen sizes.

Example:

<button class="btn btn-primary">Submit</button>
b. What is jQuery and why was it widely used in web development?

jQuery is a JavaScript library that simplifies common JavaScript tasks. It provides shorter and easier syntax for operations such as selecting HTML elements, handling events, creating animations, and making AJAX requests.

It was widely used because it made JavaScript programming easier and also provided better support for differences between web browsers.

Example:

$("#message").hide();

This code selects the element with the ID message and hides it.

c. What is React.js and what problem does it solve in frontend development?

React.js is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces. It was developed by Facebook and is widely used for creating modern and interactive web applications.

React solves the problem of managing complex and frequently changing user interfaces by allowing developers to divide the interface into reusable components.

For example, a website can have separate components for:

Header
Navigation bar
Login form
Product card
Footer

These components can be reused wherever required, which makes development and maintenance easier.
